"cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Bird Migration — Phase 2: Feature Engineering\n",
    "**Author:** Jayant Pandey  \n",
    "**Project:** Bird Migration GPS Tracking — ISI Kolkata IDEAS Internship 2026  \n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Continuation from Phase 1\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is a direct extension of `jayant_bird_migration_github.ipynb`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Phase 1 produced:** `bird_migration_with_climate.csv`\n",
    "- 61,920 GPS records across 3 White Storks (Eric, Nico, Sanne)\n",
    "- Aug 2013 to Apr 2014\n",
    "- Columns: latitude, longitude, altitude, speed_2d, direction, bird_name, date_time, unix_timestamp, day_of_year, hour, temperature, wind_speed, precipitation\n",
    "- Zero nulls\n",
    "\n",
    "**Phase 2 adds:** 33 engineered features for K-Means clustering and ML classification\n",
    "\n",
    "**Phase 2 produces:** `bird_migration_features.csv`\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "| Phase | Notebook | Output |\n",
    "|-------|----------|--------|\n",
    "| Phase 1 | `jayant_bird_migration_github.ipynb` | `bird_migration_with_climate.csv` |\n",
    "| **Phase 2** | **`phase2_feature_engineering.ipynb`** | **`bird_migration_features.csv`** |\n",
    "| Phase 3 | K-Means Clustering | `bird_migration_clustered.csv` |\n",
    "| Phase 4 | RF / XGBoost Classification | `test_predictions.csv` |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Imports done.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load Phase 1 Output\n",
    "\n",
    "Loading `bird_migration_with_climate.csv` — the final output of `jayant_bird_migration_github.ipynb`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df = pd.read_csv('bird_migration_with_climate.csv')\n",
    "df['date_time'] = pd.to_datetime(df['date_time'], utc=True)\n",
    "df = df.sort_values(['bird_name', 'date_time']).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Phase 1 output loaded successfully.')\n",
    "print('Shape:', df.shape)\n",
    "print('Columns:', df.columns.tolist())\n",
    "print('Nulls:', df.isnull().sum().sum())\n",
    "df.head(3)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### Fix 3 null values in speed_2d (Sanne, last 3 records — April 2014)\n",
    "##### Forward fill within each bird group "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "df['speed_2d'] = df.groupby('bird_name')['speed_2d'].transform(lambda x: x.ffill())\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Nulls in speed_2d after fix:', df['speed_2d'].isnull().sum())\n",
    "print('Total nulls in dataset:', df.isnull().sum().sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(df.isnull().sum()[df.isnull().sum() > 0])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df['direction'] = df.groupby('bird_name')['direction'].transform(lambda x: x.ffill())\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Nulls in direction after fix:', df['direction'].isnull().sum())\n",
    "print('Total nulls in dataset:', df.isnull().sum().sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 1.2 Duplicate Check\n",
    "Check for duplicate records — same bird at same timestamp — before feature engineering begins."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "exact_dupes = df.duplicated().sum()\n",
    "print('Exact duplicate rows:', exact_dupes)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "key_dupes = df.duplicated(subset=['bird_name', 'date_time']).sum()\n",
    "print('Duplicate bird + timestamp combinations:', key_dupes)\n",
    "\n",
    "if key_dupes > 0:\n",
    "    mask = df.duplicated(subset=['bird_name', 'date_time'], keep=False)\n",
    "    print(df[mask][['bird_name', 'date_time', 'latitude', 'longitude']].head(10))\n",
    "    df = df.drop_duplicates(subset=['bird_name', 'date_time'], keep='first').reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "    print('Duplicates removed. New shape:', df.shape)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('No duplicates found. Shape unchanged:', df.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1.3 Coordinate Validation\n",
    "#### Validating coordinate ranges\n",
    "\n",
    "Latitude is bounded by [-90°, +90°] — South Pole to North Pole.  \n",
    "Longitude is bounded by [-180°, +180°] — International Date Line to Date Line.  \n",
    "Any GPS reading outside these ranges is physically impossible and indicates a sensor error.  \n",
    "Records with invalid coordinates are removed before feature engineering."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "invalid_lat = df[(df['latitude'] < -90) | (df['latitude'] > 90)]\n",
    "invalid_lon = df[(df['longitude'] < -180) | (df['longitude'] > 180)]\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Invalid latitude values:', len(invalid_lat))\n",
    "print('Invalid longitude values:', len(invalid_lon))\n",
    "\n",
    "if len(invalid_lat) == 0 and len(invalid_lon) == 0:\n",
    "    print('All coordinates within valid geographic range.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    df = df[\n",
    "        (df['latitude'].between(-90, 90)) &\n",
    "        (df['longitude'].between(-180, 180))\n",
    "    ].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "    print('Invalid coordinates removed. New shape:', df.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Temporal Features\n",
    "\n",
    "Extract time-based features and apply cyclic (sin/cos) encoding.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why cyclic encoding?**  \n",
    "Hour 23 and Hour 0 are 1 hour apart but numerically 23 apart. Standard encoding misleads the model. Sin/cos encoding wraps the cycle correctly — 23:00 and 00:00 are treated as close."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df['hour']        = df['date_time'].dt.hour\n",
    "df['day_of_year'] = df['date_time'].dt.dayofyear\n",
    "df['month']       = df['date_time'].dt.month\n",
    "\n",
    "df['hour_sin'] = np.sin(2 * np.pi * df['hour'] / 24)\n",
    "df['hour_cos'] = np.cos(2 * np.pi * df['hour'] / 24)\n",
    "df['day_sin']  = np.sin(2 * np.pi * df['day_of_year'] / 365)\n",
    "df['day_cos']  = np.cos(2 * np.pi * df['day_of_year'] / 365)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Temporal features added.')\n",
    "df[['hour', 'day_of_year', 'hour_sin', 'hour_cos', 'day_sin', 'day_cos']].head(3)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Season Encoding\n",
    "\n",
    "Three biological seasons based on date:\n",
    "- **1 = Autumn migration** (Aug–Nov 2013) — southward journey\n",
    "- **2 = Wintering** (Dec 2013–Jan 2014) — resting in West Africa\n",
    "- **3 = Spring return** (Feb–Apr 2014) — northward journey"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def encode_season(month):\n",
    "    if month in [8, 9, 10, 11]:\n",
    "        return 1\n",
    "    elif month in [12, 1]:\n",
    "        return 2\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        return 3\n",
    "\n",
    "df['season'] = df['month'].apply(encode_season)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Season distribution:')\n",
    "print(df['season'].value_counts().sort_index())\n",
    "print('1=Autumn migration, 2=Wintering, 3=Spring return')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Time Delta\n",
    "\n",
    "Time elapsed (seconds) between consecutive GPS observations per bird.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why?** GPS is not sampled at perfectly equal intervals. Acceleration and distance features depend on elapsed time. Time_Delta gives models this context explicitly."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df['unix_timestamp'] = df['date_time'].astype(np.int64) // 10**9\n",
    "df['time_delta'] = df.groupby('bird_name')['unix_timestamp'].diff().fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Time delta stats (seconds):')\n",
    "print(df['time_delta'].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Outlier check: Time Delta (upper tail)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Time delta — high percentiles (seconds):')\n",
    "print(df['time_delta'].quantile([0.90, 0.95, 0.99, 0.999]))\n",
    "\n",
    "large_gaps = df[df['time_delta'] > df['time_delta'].quantile(0.99)]\n",
    "print(f\"\\nRecords with time_delta above 99th percentile: {len(large_gaps)}\")\n",
    "print(large_gaps[['bird_name', 'date_time', 'time_delta']].sort_values('time_delta', ascending=False).head(10))\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "plt.boxplot(df['time_delta'], vert=False)\n",
    "plt.title('Time Delta — Boxplot (seconds)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('time_delta (s)')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Kinematic Features\n",
    "\n",
    "Describe **how** the bird is moving — not just where it is.\n",
    "\n",
    "These are among the most important features because migration behaviour (active flying vs resting at stopovers) is captured in movement dynamics, not just position."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 5.1 Haversine Distance  \n",
    "**Great‑circle distance (km)** between consecutive GPS points  \n",
    "We are using the *Haversine formula* — accounts for Earth's curvature.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def haversine(lat1, lon1, lat2, lon2):\n",
    "    R = 6371.0\n",
    "    lat1, lon1, lat2, lon2 = map(np.radians, [lat1, lon1, lat2, lon2])\n",
    "    dlat = lat2 - lat1\n",
    "    dlon = lon2 - lon1\n",
    "    a = np.sin(dlat/2)**2 + np.cos(lat1) * np.cos(lat2) * np.sin(dlon/2)**2\n",
    "    return R * 2 * np.arcsin(np.sqrt(a))\n",
    "\n",
    "lat_prev = df.groupby('bird_name')['latitude'].shift(1)\n",
    "lon_prev = df.groupby('bird_name')['longitude'].shift(1)\n",
    "\n",
    "df['haversine_dist'] = haversine(\n",
    "    lat_prev.fillna(df['latitude']),\n",
    "    lon_prev.fillna(df['longitude']),\n",
    "    df['latitude'],\n",
    "    df['longitude']\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Haversine distance (km):')\n",
    "print(df['haversine_dist'].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Outlier check: Haversine Distance (upper tail)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Haversine distance — high percentiles (km):')\n",
    "print(df['haversine_dist'].quantile([0.90, 0.95, 0.99, 0.999]))\n",
    "\n",
    "large_jumps = df[df['haversine_dist'] > df['haversine_dist'].quantile(0.99)]\n",
    "print(f\"\\nRecords with haversine_dist above 99th percentile: {len(large_jumps)}\")\n",
    "print(large_jumps[['bird_name', 'date_time', 'haversine_dist', 'time_delta']].sort_values('haversine_dist', ascending=False).head(10))\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "plt.boxplot(df['haversine_dist'], vert=False)\n",
    "plt.title('Haversine Distance — Boxplot (km)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('haversine_dist (km)')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 5.2 Bearing\n",
    "Direction of travel between consecutive GPS fixes (0-360 degrees)  \n",
    "0=North, 90=East, 180=South, 270=West\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def compute_bearing(lat1, lon1, lat2, lon2):\n",
    "    lat1, lon1, lat2, lon2 = map(np.radians, [lat1, lon1, lat2, lon2])\n",
    "    dlon = lon2 - lon1\n",
    "    x = np.sin(dlon) * np.cos(lat2)\n",
    "    y = np.cos(lat1) * np.sin(lat2) - np.sin(lat1) * np.cos(lat2) * np.cos(dlon)\n",
    "    bearing = np.degrees(np.arctan2(x, y))\n",
    "    return (bearing + 360) % 360\n",
    "\n",
    "df['bearing'] = compute_bearing(\n",
    "    lat_prev.fillna(df['latitude']),\n",
    "    lon_prev.fillna(df['longitude']),\n",
    "    df['latitude'],\n",
    "    df['longitude']\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Bearing (degrees 0-360):')\n",
    "print(df['bearing'].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 5.3 Acceleration \n",
    "Rate of change in speed between consecutive observations (m/s²)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "speed_prev = df.groupby('bird_name')['speed_2d'].shift(1)\n",
    "\n",
    "df['acceleration'] = (\n",
    "    (df['speed_2d'] - speed_prev.fillna(df['speed_2d'])) /\n",
    "    df['time_delta'].replace(0, np.nan)\n",
    ").fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Acceleration (m/s²):')\n",
    "print(df['acceleration'].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Outlier check: Acceleration (upper tail, by magnitude)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Acceleration — high percentiles of |acceleration| (m/s²):')\n",
    "print(df['acceleration'].abs().quantile([0.90, 0.95, 0.99, 0.999]))\n",
    "\n",
    "accel_spikes = df[df['acceleration'].abs() > df['acceleration'].abs().quantile(0.99)]\n",
    "print(f\"\\nRecords with |acceleration| above 99th percentile: {len(accel_spikes)}\")\n",
    "print(accel_spikes[['bird_name', 'date_time', 'acceleration', 'time_delta']]\n",
    "      .reindex(accel_spikes['acceleration'].abs().sort_values(ascending=False).index)\n",
    "      .head(10))\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "plt.boxplot(df['acceleration'], vert=False)\n",
    "plt.title('Acceleration — Boxplot (m/s²)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('acceleration (m/s²)')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 5.4 Turning Rate \n",
    " How fast the bird is changing direction (degrees per second)\n",
    " High turning rate = active manoeuvring; Low = straight migration flight"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "bearing_prev = df.groupby('bird_name')['bearing'].shift(1)\n",
    "bearing_diff = (df['bearing'] - bearing_prev.fillna(df['bearing'])).abs()\n",
    "bearing_diff = bearing_diff.apply(lambda x: x if x <= 180 else 360 - x)\n",
    "\n",
    "df['turning_rate'] = (\n",
    "    bearing_diff / df['time_delta'].replace(0, np.nan)\n",
    ").fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Turning rate (degrees/second):')\n",
    "print(df['turning_rate'].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Outlier check: Turning Rate (upper tail)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Turning rate — high percentiles (deg/s):')\n",
    "print(df['turning_rate'].quantile([0.90, 0.95, 0.99, 0.999]))\n",
    "\n",
    "turn_spikes = df[df['turning_rate'] > df['turning_rate'].quantile(0.99)]\n",
    "print(f\"\\nRecords with turning_rate above 99th percentile: {len(turn_spikes)}\")\n",
    "print(turn_spikes[['bird_name', 'date_time', 'turning_rate', 'time_delta']].sort_values('turning_rate', ascending=False).head(10))\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "plt.boxplot(df['turning_rate'], vert=False)\n",
    "plt.title('Turning Rate — Boxplot (degrees/second)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('turning_rate (deg/s)')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "###  5.5 Is Resting Flag \n",
    " Binary: 1 if speed < 1 m/s (anchored/resting), 0 if actively moving\n",
    " EDA finding: 44.9% of records have speed < 1 m/s"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Resting Behaviour Feature Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "The `is_resting` feature was created using a threshold of **1.0 m/s** on horizontal speed (`speed_2d`).\n",
    "\n",
    "This threshold was selected after examining the empirical speed distribution, which showed a strong concentration of observations at low speeds followed by a gradual decline toward higher flight speeds.\n",
    "\n",
    "The resulting feature classified:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Resting observations:** 28,018 (45.25%)\n",
    "- **Active observations:** 33,902 (54.75%)\n",
    "\n",
    "The relatively balanced distribution suggests that the feature provides useful behavioural information for downstream machine learning models while remaining simple and interpretable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
