  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Outlier Flagging\n",
    "\n",
    "Identified during Phase 1 EDA:\n",
    "- Altitude: -1010m (below sea level) and +6965m (near Everest) — GPS sensor errors\n",
    "- Speed: 63.5 m/s (228 km/h) — physically impossible for a stork\n",
    "\n",
    "Flagged with binary columns rather than removed — they do not affect the classification features directly."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df['altitude_outlier'] = ((df['altitude'] < -1000) | (df['altitude'] > 6900)).astype(int)\n",
    "df['speed_outlier']    = (df['speed_2d'] > 60).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Altitude outliers flagged:', df['altitude_outlier'].sum())\n",
    "print('Speed outliers flagged:', df['speed_outlier'].sum())\n",
    "print('\\nAltitude outlier values:')\n",
    "print(df[df['altitude_outlier'] == 1][['bird_name', 'date_time', 'latitude', 'longitude', 'altitude']])\n",
    "\n",
    "print('\\nSpeed outlier value:')\n",
    "print(df[df['speed_outlier'] == 1][['bird_name', 'date_time', 'latitude', 'longitude', 'speed_2d']])\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "before_shape = df.shape\n",
    "df = df[(df['altitude_outlier'] == 0) & (df['speed_outlier'] == 0)].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "print('\\nShape before removal:', before_shape)\n",
    "print('Shape after removal :', df.shape)\n",
    "print('Rows removed         :', before_shape[0] - df.shape[0])\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Lag Features\n",
    "\n",
    "Give classical ML models short-term memory — what was the bird doing 1 and 2 timesteps ago?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why?** Unlike GRU which has built-in memory via hidden states, Random Forest and XGBoost have no memory. Lag features explicitly provide recent history as input columns — this is the standard technique to give classical ML models temporal awareness."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "for col in ['latitude', 'longitude', 'speed_2d', 'bearing']:\n",
    "    df[f'{col}_lag1'] = df.groupby('bird_name')[col].shift(1)\n",
    "    df[f'{col}_lag2'] = df.groupby('bird_name')[col].shift(2)\n",
    "\n",
    "lag_cols = [c for c in df.columns if 'lag' in c]\n",
    "df[lag_cols] = df[lag_cols].fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Lag features added:')\n",
    "print(lag_cols)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Rolling Features\n",
    "\n",
    "Moving averages and standard deviations over a window of 5 readings to smooth GPS noise.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why window=5?** GPS records are approximately every 30 minutes. A window of 5 covers ~2.5 hours — enough to capture short-term behaviour patterns without smoothing away meaningful variation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "WINDOW = 5\n",
    "df['rolling_mean_speed']   = df.groupby('bird_name')['speed_2d'].transform(\n",
    "    lambda x: x.rolling(WINDOW, min_periods=1).mean()\n",
    ")\n",
    "df['rolling_std_speed']    = df.groupby('bird_name')['speed_2d'].transform(\n",
    "    lambda x: x.rolling(WINDOW, min_periods=1).std()\n",
    ").fillna(0)\n",
    "df['rolling_mean_heading'] = df.groupby('bird_name')['bearing'].transform(\n",
    "    lambda x: x.rolling(WINDOW, min_periods=1).mean()\n",
    ")\n",
    "print('Rolling features added (window=5).')\n",
    "df[['rolling_mean_speed', 'rolling_std_speed', 'rolling_mean_heading']].describe()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print('temperature' in df.columns)\n",
    "print('wind_speed' in df.columns)\n",
    "print(df.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Environmental Change Features\n",
    "\n",
    "Rate of change in environmental conditions between consecutive GPS readings.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why?** A bird deciding to migrate responds to changing weather, not just current weather. Temperature dropping 5°C overnight is more informative than absolute temperature = 15°C."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df['altitude_change'] = df.groupby('bird_name')['altitude'].diff().fillna(0)\n",
    "print('Altitude change feature added.')\n",
    "df[['altitude_change']].describe()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df.drop(columns=['temperature', 'wind_speed', 'precipitation',\n",
    "                 'temperature_change', 'wind_speed_change'], \n",
    "        errors='ignore', inplace=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Final Feature Summary"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SPATIAL     = ['latitude', 'longitude', 'altitude']\n",
    "KINEMATIC   = ['speed_2d', 'bearing', 'acceleration', 'turning_rate',\n",
    "               'haversine_dist', 'is_resting']\n",
    "TEMPORAL    = ['hour', 'day_of_year', 'month', 'hour_sin', 'hour_cos',\n",
    "               'day_sin', 'day_cos', 'season', 'time_delta']\n",
    "LAG         = ['latitude_lag1', 'latitude_lag2',\n",
    "               'longitude_lag1', 'longitude_lag2',\n",
    "               'speed_2d_lag1', 'speed_2d_lag2',\n",
    "               'bearing_lag1', 'bearing_lag2']\n",
    "ROLLING     = ['rolling_mean_speed', 'rolling_std_speed', 'rolling_mean_heading']\n",
    "ENVIRONMENT = ['altitude_change']\n",
    "CATEGORICAL = ['bird_name']\n",
    "FLAGS       = ['altitude_outlier', 'speed_outlier']\n",
    "\n",
    "ALL_FEATURES = SPATIAL + KINEMATIC + TEMPORAL + LAG + ROLLING + ENVIRONMENT + CATEGORICAL + FLAGS\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=== FEATURE ENGINEERING SUMMARY ===')\n",
    "print(f'Spatial:          {len(SPATIAL):>3} features  — where the bird is')\n",
